WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.357 --> 00:00:01.542
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.542 --> 00:00:04.456
- [Narrator] Our founding
fathers were booze hounds.

00:00:04.456 --> 00:00:05.373
(clinking glasses)

00:00:05.373 --> 00:00:07.172
So much so, that Benjamin
Franklin published

00:00:07.172 --> 00:00:11.339
a dictionary of 228 words
that all describe one thing,

00:00:12.548 --> 00:00:15.090
being blind drunk in the 13 colonies.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.134
- [Founding Father] We love to drink.

00:00:17.134 --> 00:00:19.688
- [Narrator] Colonial Americans
were perpetually bombed,

00:00:19.688 --> 00:00:21.588
especially since water wasn't always

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.879
clean and accessible.

00:00:22.879 --> 00:00:23.768
- [Man] Aww, gross.

00:00:23.768 --> 00:00:25.521
- [Narrator] Many of our
nations most respected men

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:28.644
could be found with a
glass or two in hand.

00:00:28.644 --> 00:00:30.594
In fact, Thomas Jefferson drafted

00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:31.986
the Declaration of Independence

00:00:31.986 --> 00:00:32.941
- [Jefferson] Ah, yes. Oh, whoops.

00:00:32.941 --> 00:00:34.195
- [Narrator] while drunk on Madeira.

00:00:34.195 --> 00:00:35.948
George Washington racked
up an epic bar tab

00:00:35.948 --> 00:00:39.245
of over 160 bottles for just 54 delegates.

00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:40.394
- [Franklin] It's on me.

00:00:40.394 --> 00:00:41.950
- [Narrator] And John
Adams went on a seven week

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.742
binge, drinking six hours a
night with younger congressmen.

00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:46.284
- [Adams] Keep drinking, keep drinking.

00:00:46.284 --> 00:00:47.619
- [Narrator] So Franklin
took a stab at his peers

00:00:47.619 --> 00:00:49.918
and published the terms
he overheard at local pubs

00:00:49.918 --> 00:00:51.624
in the Drinkers Dictionary.

00:00:51.624 --> 00:00:54.260
Here's what they said.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.465
- I've got corns in my head.

00:00:56.465 --> 00:00:58.915
- Oh, go eat a pudding bag, Thomas.

00:00:58.915 --> 00:01:00.215
- You're one to talk Washington

00:01:00.215 --> 00:01:02.142
You're as dizzy as a goose.

00:01:02.142 --> 00:01:03.338
- I'm jambled.

00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:06.647
- My goodness Hamilton,
you've got a brass eye today.

00:01:06.647 --> 00:01:08.690
- Well, the King was his cousin.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.940
- Clearly gentlemen, you're all wasted.

